      "text": "3.3 The Riordan group and the Sheffer group",
      "html": null,
      "level": 1,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11710947712418301,
        "y0": 0.8423724747474748,
        "x1": 0.8842581699346406,
        "y1": 0.9211666666666667
      },
      "text": "The expansion of the polynomial fλ(θ;α) via the Sheffer A-type zero sequence (Sheffer, 1939) introduced in Section 3.1 is encompassed in the modern theory of umbral interpolation (Costabile et al., 2025) initiated by the work Roman and Rota (1978) and the book of Roman (1984) as the main reference for further developments. Consider a sequence of polynomials {si(θ)}∞i=0 (where si(θ) is of degree i) for a pair of characteristic exponential power series (d(t),h(t)) (overlap in notation with the previous section is intentional) with real-valued coefficients provided that d0 ̸= 0, h0 = 0",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
